## First design attempt — caught its own bug before shipping

The first scanner jumped past a matched function's WHOLE body once its end
line was computed, to avoid re-scanning it. That silently skipped every
function declared INSIDE that body. Found by comparing against a naive
unique-name grep of `function name(` across the whole file (no string/
comment awareness, so it over-counts from comments/strings, but never
UNDER-counts real top-level+nested declarations): the body-skipping
scanner returned fewer names (534 for app.js) than the naive one (849
unique names) — the wrong direction, since a context-aware scanner should
only ever REMOVE false positives (comment/string matches), never real
declarations. Redesigned to separate "find declaration start positions"
(never skipped) from "compute one declaration's end line" (an independent
nested scan). Re-ran: 692 for app.js, confirmed nested functions
(getActiveRole etc.) now present.

